  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlways directed at another person — you {急|せ}かす someone else. Often appears in the passive form {急|せ}かされる (to be rushed by someone). Carries a mildly negative nuance of unwanted pressure.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb ending in す. Transitive — takes を for the person being rushed: Xを{急|せ}かす.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {急|せ}かさないで: don't rush me\n- {急|せ}かされる: to be rushed (passive)\n- {返事|へんじ}を{急|せ}かす: to press for a reply",
